WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.840
A prison gate opens.

2
00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:05.120
Ten people walk out, sentences served.

3
00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.540
A year goes by.

4
00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:11.120
Four of the ten commit another crime,
and are convicted or cautioned for it.

5
00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:13.290
That's close to the real figure.

6
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:18.300
For adults released from custody, 40.6
per cent were proven to reoffend within

7
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.410
a year.

8
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.560
If prison doesn't stop so
many people offending again,

9
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.310
what might work better?

10
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:29.110
In this mission, you'll meet recidivism,
and the jobs punishment is meant to do:

11
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:34.070
deter, incapacitate, rehabilitate
and give retribution.

12
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.630
You'll weigh up what prison does
well, and where it goes wrong.

13
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.470
Then you'll put the
alternatives to the test.

14
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.210
Your mission: find out what might work better
than prison at stopping people offending

15
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:45.790
again.
